    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186133894,
      "id": "2900032e-de37-5c3e-a03a-be6b892976db",
      "title": "Evaluating Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions Over Space Curves"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "25d5af65-10cf-577f-8576-0cc5d0fcc957",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left(2 x\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left(t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in [0,1]$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t,\\qquad y=- t - 1,\\qquad z=2 t + 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =2 x\\,\\mathbf{i}+- z\\,\\mathbf{j}+2 y\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\left(2 \\left(t\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- \\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 \\left(- t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =2 t\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- 2 t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(- 2 t - 2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\,\\mathbf{i}+-\\,\\mathbf{j}+2\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(2 t\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 t - 1\\right)\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 t - 2\\right)\\left(2\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2 t\\right)+\\left(1\\right)+\\left(2 t\\right)+\\left(-4\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 4 t\\right) \\\\ & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r} & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(-3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- 3 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- 3 \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- 3 \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(-3\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
