    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9c19fc9e-a979-5f05-8dd7-afde70edd520",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left(- y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(- x\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in [0,1]$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t - 1,\\qquad y=- 2 t,\\qquad z=t - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =- y\\,\\mathbf{i}+z\\,\\mathbf{j}+- x\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\left(- \\left(- 2 t\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- \\left(t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =2 t\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(1 - t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\,\\mathbf{i}+-2\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(2 t\\right)\\left(1\\right)+\\left(t - 1\\right)\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(1 - t\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2 t\\right)+\\left(2\\right)+\\left(- 2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(1\\right)+\\left(- t\\right) \\\\ & =3 - t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r} & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(3 - t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- \\frac{t^{2}}{2} + 3 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- \\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2}}{2} + 3 \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- \\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2} + 3 \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
