    "question": {
      ":question/id": "406caa2c-15dd-51a0-bd65-f5df535c5811",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left(z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(- y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left(- t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in [0,1]$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=- t,\\qquad y=t - 1,\\qquad z=- 2 t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =z\\,\\mathbf{i}+- 2 x\\,\\mathbf{j}+- y\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\left(\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(- t\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- \\left(t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =- 2 t\\,\\mathbf{i}+2 t\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(1 - t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =-\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\,\\mathbf{j}+-2\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\left(-1\\right)+\\left(2 t\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(1 - t\\right)\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2 t\\right)+\\left(2 t\\right)+\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 t\\right) \\\\ & =6 t - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r} & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(6 t - 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[3 t^{2} - 2 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(3 \\left(1\\right)^{2} - 2 \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(3 \\left(0\\right)^{2} - 2 \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
